        <type><ref refid="struct_f_skeleton_options_data" kindref="compound">FSkeletonOptionsData</ref></type>
        <definition>FSkeletonOptionsData UPrimaryCharacterData::GetCharacterSkeleton</definition>
        <argsstring>(const bool bForceMasculine=false, const bool bForceFeminine=false) const</argsstring>
        <name>GetCharacterSkeleton</name>
        <qualifiedname>UPrimaryCharacterData::GetCharacterSkeleton</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const bool</type>
          <declname>bForceMasculine</declname>
          <defval>false</defval>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const bool</type>
          <declname>bForceFeminine</declname>
          <defval>false</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Returns a random skeleton &amp; animation instance from the skeleton options. Will return a feminine or masculine skeleton if one boolean is true. Will disregard sex is both booleans are true or both false. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>bForceMasculine</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>If TRUE, only masculine options will be considered </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>bForceFeminine</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>If TRUE, only feminine options will be considered </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The mesh and anim instance being used by this character </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
